al-arc-task-94779289.md\",\n \"content\": \"# Continual-ARC task 94779289\\n\\nPuzzle rule learned from demos and solved test: In a uniform background grid, sparse pixels of a contrasting color mark endpoints of horizontal/vertical lines. Extend the matching-color line segment between same-row/same-column marker pixels by recoloring intervening background cells to 2; keep all original marker pixels unchanged. Do not extend beyond endpoints, and only fill rows/columns where marker endpoints actually exist.\\n\\nDemo 1: 8x9 background 1, markers 8; output filled between each aligned pair of 8s with color 2 (horizontal and vertical). Demo 2: 19x29 background 3, markers 8; horizontal row4 and row18 gaps between marker endpoints are filled 2; vertical columns4 and 26 segments between marker endpoints filled 2.\\n\\nSolved test 11x26 background 9, markers 3. Correct output preserved all 3s and filled 2s between aligned markers: horizontal row 5 (1-indexed) col11 to col23 between 3s; row7 had only its runs untouched (no horizontal additions beyond matching markers); vertical col11 filled rows5-7 between endpoint at row5 and row9? Actual solved output: col11 rows6-7 were 2; vertical col23 rows7-8 were 2; horizontal row9 cols12-19 and 21-22 were 2. Exact answer was accepted. Key operational lesson: interpret each pair of marker endpoints in a row/column as an interval; fill all cells between consecutive matching endpoints, preserving markers. Use explicit carefully counted grid dimensions; previous incorrect submissions had mistakes in which intervals were included/excluded and one malformed row.\\n\"\n}","t":1792570028.592,"stored":["memory/continual-arc-task-94779289.md"],"output":"Successfully wrote 1559 bytes to /home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-openclawlearner-1792545336/attempts/fca3304bc44e41ab9d84755e7ae3ff98/system/state/workspace/memory/continual-arc-task-94779289.md"},{"type":"reasoning","text":"**Finishing action JSON**\n\nI need to finis